<title>CANADA: Canada Nov industrial price index falls 0.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Canada Nov industrial price index falls 0.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Canada on Friday issued the following economic indicators for November.</p>
<p>INDUSTRIAL PRODUCT PRICE INDEX   Month-on-Month   Year-on-Year</p>
<p>    Change				 -0.2		 -0.5</p>
<p>					   Nov 96    Oct 96    Nov 95</p>
<p>    Index (base 100=86)	    129.0     129.1     129.7</p>
<p>INDUSTRIAL PRODUCT PRICE INDEX   Month-on-Month   Year-on-Year</p>
<p>    Intermediate goods		 -0.2		 -2.3</p>
<p>    Finished goods		     -0.2		 +2.5</p>
<p>The IPPI reflects the prices producers receive as goods leave their plants.</p>
<p>(For more information, contact Statistics Canada's Client Services Unit at (613) 951-3350 or fax: (613) 951-2848)</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
